.TH TELEDDNS 1 "September 2026" "teleddns 0.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teleddns \- advanced DDNS client with Netlink support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teleddns
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teleddns
is an advanced DDNS client with daemonization support (as a systemd service)
or one-shot running capability. When running in daemon mode, it listens for
Netlink messages and pools updates to minimize both DDNS convergence time
and resource usage.
.PP
The client is compatible with teleddns-server and supports both IPv4 and IPv6
address updates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to the configuration file.
Default: \fI/etc/teleddns/teleddns.yaml\fR
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-oneshot
Do not daemonize. Run just one DDNS update and hooks, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity. Can be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Decrease logging verbosity. Can be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is in YAML format. A sample configuration file is
installed at \fI/usr/share/doc/teleddns/teleddns.yaml.sample\fR.
.PP
To configure teleddns:
.RS
.nf
mkdir -p /etc/teleddns
cp /usr/share/doc/teleddns/teleddns.yaml.sample /etc/teleddns/teleddns.yaml
# Edit the file with your DDNS credentials
.fi
.RE
.PP
Key configuration options:
.TP
.B ddns_url
The DDNS update URL including credentials in the form
\fIhttps://user:pass@host/ddns/update\fR
.TP
.B hostname
The FQDN to update (e.g., \fImyhost.ddns.example.com\fR)
.TP
.B enable_ipv4
Enable IPv4 address updates (true/false)
.TP
.B enable_ipv6
Enable IPv6 address updates (true/false)
.TP
.B interfaces
List of interfaces to monitor. Use '*' for all interfaces.
.TP
.B hooks
Optional list of hooks to execute after address changes.
.PP
Update timing (all optional; durations are written as \fI'5s'\fR, \fI'15min'\fR,
\fI'12h'\fR). The defaults keep the client inside the 60 updates per hour and
address family that teleddns-server permits:
.TP
.B ddns_settle_delay
Debounce window after an address change before publishing. Default: \fI5s\fR
.TP
.B ddns_min_interval
Hard minimum between two updates of the same family. Default: \fI60s\fR
.TP
.B ddns_max_updates_per_hour
Sliding-window cap per family. Default: \fI30\fR
.TP
.B ddns_retry_min\fR, \fBddns_retry_max
Exponential back-off bounds after a transient failure.
Defaults: \fI60s\fR, \fI1h\fR
.TP
.B ddns_retry_ratelimit_min
Back-off floor after an \fIabuse\fR (HTTP 429) answer. Default: \fI15min\fR
.TP
.B ddns_resync_period
Re-publish unconditionally this often; \fI0s\fR disables. Default: \fI12h\fR
.TP
.B ddns_kernel_poll_period
Periodically re-read all addresses from the kernel. Default: \fI0s\fR (off)
.TP
.B http_timeout
Timeout for a single DDNS request. Default: \fI30s\fR
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM\fR, \fBSIGINT\fR, \fBSIGHUP
Shut down gracefully.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/teleddns/teleddns.yaml
Main configuration file (created by user)
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/teleddns/teleddns.yaml.sample
Sample configuration file
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful operation
.TP
.B 1
The configuration file could not be read, contains an unknown key, or failed
validation. The message names the offending key and line.
.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred. In \fB\-\-oneshot\fR mode this also covers a DDNS update
that did not go through.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a one-shot update:
.RS
.nf
teleddns -o
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with increased verbosity:
.RS
.nf
teleddns -v
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a custom configuration file:
.RS
.nf
teleddns -c /path/to/config.yaml
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
\fIDYNDNS2.md\fR in the source distribution documents the protocol the client
speaks and how it reacts to each server answer.
